  "playVsComputer": "Play vs computer",
  "rulesShortBody": "Each player has 15 checkers. Checkers move from 24 towards 1 according to the dice. Land on a lone opponent checker and you send it to the bar; a point with two or more checkers is blocked. Once all your checkers are home (1–6), you start bearing off. The first to bear off all 15 checkers wins. If the opponent has borne off none — mars (×2); if they still have a checker on the bar or in your home — koks (×3).",
  "rulesLongBody": "All 15 checkers start on the head (point 24). There is no hitting: you can't move to a point with an opponent checker. Each turn you may take only one checker from the head (except 6-6, 4-4 and 3-3 on the first roll). You can't block 6 points in a row unless an opponent checker is ahead of them. Once all your checkers are home, you start bearing off. If the opponent has borne off none — mars (×2); if one of their checkers hasn't yet passed your home — koks (×3)."
